# You're in the Oddly-Angled Room, Zork's monument to the national
# pastime. Walkthroughs say to hunt for the club "usually east or
# west," but the hunt is an illusion: until the puzzle is solved
# this maze cannot be mapped, because every exit is a trapdoor to a
# random room. Probed empirically under this seed, all sixty-four
# two-move combinations land in the same place -- home plate, where
# the club lies by the diamond-shaped window. Two moves of any kind
# arrive.

nw. se.

# LEAVE THE CLUB ON THE GROUND -- for now. The run below advances
# identically without it, and its bulk is exactly what costs you
# the violin at the load limit (shades of the teapot). The club IS
# wanted later, at the aquarium, but the solved maze stays walkable,
# so we return for it once our hands are free. Now run the bases
# from home plate. The window in
# the floor is the progress meter, climbing from flickering dimly
# through dimly glowing, glowing, and glowing brightly to glowing
# serenely. The "strange rusty squeal" on the last move is the
# reward, rendered in sound: back at the stairway, the floor has
# swung down to reveal a secret passage -- down to the Cerberus
# Room, where the endgame waits.

se. ne. nw. sw

# Back out the way we came to collect the stash from the Cobwebby
# Corridor. (This route was right all along; only the club in hand
# made "get all treasures" choke on the violin.)

s
u. n. n
sw

# Shed the last of the ballast. Neither the newspaper nor the
# matchbook has any further part to play, and the corridor keeps
# them safe if that ever proves wrong.

drop newspaper and matchbook
get all treasures

sw
give candy to lizard
unlock door with key
open door
s. w
turn off lantern
put red on ruby stand
put blue on sapphire stand
w

# The club's ambush: the walkthroughs now want it thrown at the
# aquarium -- the same club whose bulk cost us the violin, which is
# why it stayed at home plate. No harm done: solving the diamond
# didn't just open the secret passage, it tamed the maze. The exits
# are real now, and home plate sits one step north of the stairway
# entrance. Walk back, fetch the club, and return; the load works
# this time because the candy went to the lizard and both spheres
# are parked on their stands.

turn on lantern
e. e. n. n
ne. s. s. d
n
get club
s. u. n. n
sw. sw. s. w. w

# The reward for the errand: the club shatters the aquarium, the
