# "But one treasure is yet to be given!" The demon keeps honest
# books, and the missing entry is the golden dragon statuette --
# still nestled in its chest back at the Dragon's Lair, because
# this release's chest does not open on the first try. "The hinges
# are very rusty," the game says; "you can probably open it if you
# try again." No walkthrough tries again, and the princess waking
# in the same breath distracts everyone from noticing that "get
# statuette" bounced off a still-closed lid. Nor can it be fixed
# at the source: one extra turn there reshuffles every die roll
# after it -- the princess wanders off unfollowed, and the Wizard,
# merciful no longer, Filches the statuette into his trophy
# cabinet. So we run the errand now, at the end of the recorded
# timeline, when the only thing left to disturb is the demon's
# patience.

n. e. n. n
ne. nw
n. n. n
open chest
get statuette
s. s. s
se. sw. sw. s. w. s

# "This will do for my fee. 'Tis a paltry hoard, but as you have
# done me a small service by loosing me from this wizard, it will
# suffice." Satisfied at last.

give statuette to demon

# You could also do: DEMON, GIVE ME WAND

demon, kill wizard

